  "body": "## What changed\n\nv5.0.0 renamed the distribution to `my-claude-code` and the wheel to `my_claude_code-<ver>-py3-none-any.whl`, but the published installers and the self-updater still referenced `free-claude-code`/`free_claude_code`. Every fresh install 404'd on the release wheel (`Page not found` → `WebException`), and the self-updater could no longer find its own installed package or receipt.\n\n### 1. Installers + self-updater point at the renamed package\n\n`scripts/install.sh`, `scripts/install.ps1`, and `release_updates.PACKAGE_NAME` now use `my-claude-code` / `my_claude_code`. The legacy `fcc-*` commands still exist as aliases (pyproject ships both families), so the existing `fcc-server --version` verification is unchanged.\n\n### 2. install.sh digest extraction read the release BODY, not the asset\n\nGitHub places `body` before `assets` in the payload, and the v5.0.0 notes repeat the wheel's sha256 as prose. `grep -m1 '\"digest\"'` landed on that prose, producing a **checksum mismatch on every install**. The awk now grabs the digest only from the asset whose name matches the wheel we download. The PS installer already read `$wheelAsset[0].digest` and was correct.\n\n### 3. Restart rebind could fail on a lingering socket (WSL)\n\nThe new process's startup wait was a fixed 5s; if the old listener had not released, the new process gave up and died, leaving the service unavailable. The startup wait now scales to the configured graceful-shutdown budget, and the POSIX handoff waits for the port to free before `execv`.\n\n## Verification\n\nReal isolated `install.ps1` run (throwaway `UV_TOOL_DIR`/`HOME`):\n\n```\n+ curl -fsSL https://github.com/FiredMosquito831/free-claude-code/releases/download/v5.0.0/my_claude_code-5.0.0-py3-none-any.whl -o ...\nVerified FCC v5.0.0 release wheel SHA-256.\nInstalled 18 executables: fcc-..., mcc-..., my-claude-code\nFree Claude Code 5.0.0 is installed and verified.\n```\n\n`install.sh --dry-run` shows the correct wheel URL and digest for both `latest` and `--version` paths.\n\n`ruff format`/`check` and `ty` clean. Full suite: **3657 passed**, only the 16 documented pre-existing PowerShell installer/uninstaller failures — **identical on unmodified `main`** (verified against the baseline worktree), so not regressions.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- The `install.sh` path was verified end-to-end only as a dry-run on Windows (Git Bash path translation defeats a live POSIX-path install); the full live install was verified via `install.ps1`. Linux CI exercises the POSIX harness including the new digest regression test.\n- The self-updater (`release_updates.PACKAGE_NAME`) now matches `my-claude-code`; an install that is *already* running v5.0.0's code (with the old `free-claude-code` PACKAGE_NAME) will self-report correctly after this update, but the update from 5.0.0 → 5.0.1 should be taken via the install script once if the dashboard can't detect it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
