    "message": "fix: 5.0.1 repair installer wheel/distribution names, digest extraction, and restart rebind\n\nThe v5.0.0 rebrand renamed the distribution to my-claude-code and the wheel to\nmy_claude_code-<ver>-py3-none-any.whl, but the published installers and the\nself-updater still referenced free-claude-code/free_claude_code. Every fresh\ninstall 404'd on the release wheel, and the self-updater could no longer find\nits own installed package or receipt.\n\nThree defects fixed:\n\n1. Installers + self-updater pointed at the old distribution. install.sh,\n   install.ps1, and release_updates.PACKAGE_NAME now use my-claude-code /\n   my_claude_code, so the wheel resolves and uv installs the renamed package.\n   The legacy fcc-* commands still exist as aliases (pyproject ships both\n   families), so the existing fcc-server --version verification is unchanged.\n\n2. install.sh's digest extraction read the release BODY, not the asset. GitHub\n   places body before assets in the payload, and the v5.0.0 notes repeat the\n   wheel's sha256 as prose. grep -m1 '\"digest\"' landed on that prose, producing\n   a checksum mismatch on every install. The awk now grabs the digest only from\n   the asset whose name matches the wheel we download. The PS installer already\n   read asset[0].digest and was correct.\n\n3. Restart rebind could fail on a lingering socket (WSL). The new process's\n   startup wait was a fixed 5s; if the old listener had not released, the new\n   process gave up and died, leaving the service unavailable. The startup wait\n   now scales to the graceful-shutdown budget, and the POSIX handoff waits for\n   the port to free before execv.\n\nVerified: real isolated install.ps1 run downloads the my_claude_code wheel,\nverifies sha256 8a491ce6..., installs all 18 executables, and reports\n\"Free Claude Code 5.0.0 is installed and verified.\" install.sh dry-run shows\nthe correct wheel URL and digest for both latest and --version. ruff/ty clean;\nfull suite 3657 passed with only the 16 documented pre-existing PowerShell\ninstaller/uninstaller failures (identical on unmodified main).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
